## Flavor definition schema
##
## A "flavor" is one reproducible check configuration: a base OS, a way of
## building R, and the environment R CMD check runs under. Most flavors
## correspond to one CRAN "additional issue" kind
## (https://cran.r-project.org/web/checks/check_issue_kinds.html).
##
## Flavor files are `flavors/<FLAVOR_ID>.conf` and are sourced by bash, both on
## the host (bin/rcheck) and inside the container (docker/lib/flavor.sh). They
## must contain nothing but variable assignments -- no commands, no
## conditionals -- so that they stay trivially auditable and machine-readable.
##
## `tests/test-flavors.sh` enforces this schema: every key below is checked for
## presence and, where applicable, for a legal value, and any key *not* listed
## below is rejected (so typos fail the test suite rather than being silently
## ignored).
##
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Identity
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
##
## FLAVOR_ID        Required. Must equal the file's basename. Used for image
##                  tags, build directories and result file names.
## FLAVOR_TITLE     Required. One-line human description.
## CRAN_ISSUE_KIND  Required, may be empty. The CRAN additional-issue kind this
##                  flavor reproduces, spelled exactly as CRAN spells it (e.g.
##                  `noLD`, `gcc-UBSAN`). Empty for control flavors that
##                  correspond to a regular check flavor rather than an
##                  additional issue. This is the join key used by
##                  `rcheck compare` against CRAN's published results.
## CRAN_HOST_OS     Required. The OS CRAN actually runs this check on, per the
##                  CRAN team page. Recorded so that the *fidelity gap* between
##                  our container and CRAN is explicit rather than implied;
##                  where it differs from BASE_IMAGE, say why in NOTES.
## TIER             Required. 1 | 2 | 3 -- implementation priority, see
##                  docs/qa-improvement-plan.md.
## STATUS           Required. implemented | experimental | planned
##                  `implemented`  builds and checks are wired up end to end.
##                  `experimental` wired up but the configuration has not been
##                                 validated against CRAN's own results yet.
##                  `planned`      declared for the record; not usable.
## REFERENCE        Required, may be empty. Authoritative source for the
##                  configuration (R-admin manual section, bdr README URL).
##
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Base image
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
##
## BASE_FAMILY      Required. debian | fedora. Only `debian` is implemented;
##                  see docs/architecture.md ADR-0005 for the Fedora gap.
## BASE_IMAGE       Required. Registry path without tag, e.g. docker.io/debian.
## BASE_TAG         Required. e.g. unstable, testing, trixie.
## APT_COMPONENTS   Debian archive components to enable, default `main`. Set to
##                  e.g. `main contrib non-free` for flavors whose libraries are
##                  not in main (Intel MKL). Recorded per flavor because
##                  enabling non-free changes what the image legally is.
##                  The digest for BASE_IMAGE:BASE_TAG is *not* stored here --
##                  it lives in pins/base-images.json so that one pin refresh
##                  updates every flavor sharing a base. See tools/pin-images.sh.
##
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Building R
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
##
## R_BUILD_SYSDEPS  Space-separated apt packages installed into the image on top
##                  of `apt build-dep r-base` (e.g. an alternative BLAS, a
##                  sanitizer runtime, valgrind).
## R_BUILD_METHOD   cran-qa | configure
##                  `cran-qa`   run CRAN's own build-R script from the QA SVN
##                              checkout. Highest fidelity, but build-R sets
##                              some of its own compiler flags, so flavors that
##                              need to control CC/CXX cannot rely on it.
##                  `configure` run ./configure && make ourselves, so the
##                              flavor fully determines the toolchain. Required
##                              for every sanitizer and for noLD.
##                  See docs/architecture.md ADR-0003.
## R_CONFIGURE_ARGS Extra arguments appended to ./configure.
## R_CC R_CXX R_FC  Compiler commands, including any flags that must be baked
##                  into the compiler driver so that *packages* inherit them
##                  (this is how sanitizer instrumentation reaches package code:
##                  R records CC/CXX at configure time and R CMD INSTALL reuses
##                  them). Empty means "distribution default".
## R_CFLAGS R_CXXFLAGS R_FFLAGS R_LDFLAGS R_MAIN_LDFLAGS
##                  Passed through config.site.
##
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Running the check
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
##
## CHECK_RENVIRON   Newline-separated `VAR=value` lines appended to
##                  ~/.R/check.Renviron. This is the mechanism CRAN itself uses
##                  to configure checks, and R CMD check reads it natively, so
##                  it works regardless of how the surrounding QA script is
##                  invoked. Prefer this over CHECK_EXTRA_ARGS.
## CHECK_RUNTIME_ENV
##                  Newline-separated `VAR=value` lines exported into the
##                  environment of the check process itself (ASAN_OPTIONS,
##                  UBSAN_OPTIONS, ...). Unlike CHECK_RENVIRON these are needed
##                  by the sanitizer runtimes, which are not R settings.
## CHECK_EXTRA_ARGS Extra arguments forwarded to the check driver script.
##                  UNVERIFIED: whether CRAN's check_CRAN_incoming forwards
##                  unknown options to R CMD check has not been confirmed --
##                  see docs/open-questions.md Q4. Use CHECK_RENVIRON instead
##                  wherever an equivalent environment variable exists.
##
